{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator-verified root cause + stopgap (supersedes my concurrency suspicion above): the 400 only affects models with a NATIVE structured-output capability row (sonnet-4-6, haiku-4-5-*), which send Bedrock a JSON Schema compiled as a decoding grammar; the Pass-2 verification contracts (e.g. plan_review_verification, 31 optional params) exceed Anthropic's grammar-complexity budget - 'Grammar compilation timed out' after ~185s. opus-4-8 is a deliberate non-row so it stays prompted: the exact failing contract succeeds on opus-4-8 prompted in 7.8s vs 400 after 185.3s on sonnet-4-6. Stopgap in use by this session: export REBAR_LLM_STANDARD_MODEL=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8 (env outranks config; trivial-class left alone - its 459-722B contracts compile fine). NOT a new default (frontier cost). Permanent fix direction: the schema-complexity/staleness check for native structured-output selection should reject or downgrade contracts that exceed the provider grammar budget instead of failing the whole verify step closed - relates to df3a-5a7a-01e5-43f6 (schema-blind structured-output selection). My earlier concurrency hypothesis is refuted as the primary trigger: serial sonnet runs fail identically."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785957421524986001,"uuid":"30bf1951-047b-4546-93d0-e842a9e3fdc7"}